efore, on Monday, he reads one book (the first one) which is 20 pages. Then on Tuesday, reads the second book with 12 pages. So how many pages is the third book on Wednesday? If the first two are 20 and 12, then total pages from Monday to Tuesday would be 20 + 12 = 32. Then there's the third book, which by total pages is 51 - 32 = 19? Wait, but the problem says he has read a total of 51 from Monday to Wednesday, so adding up 32 (Monday-Tuesday) plus Wednesday's pages equals 51. So Wednesday's pages should be 51 - 32 = 19. So answer is 19?\n\nBut let me check again. Let me confirm the numbers. Monday: 20 pages, Tuesday: 12 pages. Total so far: 20 + 12 = 32. Wednesday: 51 - 32 = 19. Yes, that seems correct. Therefore, the answer is 19. \n\nWait, but let me make sure there's no trick here. The problem says \"he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday\". So starting from Monday, he reads the first book on Monday (20 pages), then Tuesday (second book 12 pages), and Wednesday. So adding all three: 20 + 12 + x = 51, solving for x gives 51 - 20 -12 = 19. Yep, that's right. So he read 19 pages on Wednesday. \n\nTherefore, the number of pages he read on Wednesday is 19. So the answer should be \\boxed{19}.\n</think>\n\nNico borrowed 3 books on Monday. He read 20 pages on Monday's first book and 12 pages on Tuesday's second book, totaling 32 pages from Monday to Tuesday. Since he read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, the number of pages he read on Wednesday is:\n\n$$\n51 - (20 + 12) = 19\n$$\n\nFinal Answer: $\\boxed{19}$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?", "answer": "From Monday to Tuesday, Nico reads a total of 20 + 12 = <<20+12=32>>32 pages.\nOn Wednesday, he read a total of 51 - 32 = <<51-32=19>>19 pages.\n#### 19", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["19"], "solution": "19"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 74035, 31632, 1811, 220, 18, 6467, 504, 279, 6733, 389, 7014, 13, 220, 1913, 7014, 11, 566, 15804, 279, 1156, 2311, 448, 264, 2790, 315, 220, 17, 15, 6816, 13, 220, 1913, 7589, 11, 566, 15804, 279], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 975, 1526, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 2055, 11, 74035, 31632, 1811, 220, 18, 6467, 389, 7014, 13, 5005, 566, 15804, 1817, 2311, 448, 2155, 2150, 14579, 25, 220, 17, 15, 6816, 389, 7014, 11, 220, 16, 17, 6816, 389, 7589, 11, 323, 1221, 1045, 3311, 389, 7920, 13, 576, 2790, 6816, 1349, 504, 7014]}
