12 + 3 = 15. So ceilings left would be 28 - 15 = 13? Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the second step. Let me think again. First week: total 28, 12 painted, so 28 - 12 = 16. Then second week, he paints 1/4 the number he painted this week. So the number painted this week is 12. So 12 divided by 4 is 3. Therefore, next week he paints 3. So from the 16 left after first week, he paints 3, so 16 - 3 = 13. So yes, 13 ceilings left to paint after next week. Therefore, answer is 13. So in boxed form, \\boxed{13}\n\nWait, but let me cross-validate to make sure I didn't skip anything. Let's do the math again:\n\nTotal ceilings = 28.\n\nWeek 1: painted 12, so left 28 - 12 = 16.\n\nWeek 2: he paints 1/4 of 12, which is 3, so 16 - 3 = 13.\n\nYes, that seems correct. Alternatively, another way: the problem says next week he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. If this week he painted 12, next week he paints (1/4)*12 = 3. Therefore, total ceilings painted is 12 + 3 = 15. Therefore, left is 28 - 15 = 13. Yep, same answer. So the answer is 13. Therefore, \\boxed{13} is the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nMichelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints **12** ceilings. Thus, after the week, the number of ceilings left to paint is:\n\n$$\n28 - 12 = 16\n$$\n\nNext week, he paints $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of the 12 ceilings he painted this week. This is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4} \\times 12 = 3\n$$\n\nFinally, after next week, the number of ceilings left to paint is:\n\n$$\n16 - 3 = 13\n$$\n\n$$\n\\boxed{13}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?", "answer": "After this week, Michelangelo will have 28-12=<<28-12=16>>16 more ceilings to paint.\nNext week, Michelangelo will paint 12/4=<<12/4=3>>3 ceilings.\nMichelangelo will have 16-3=<<16-3=13>>13 more ceilings to paint.\n#### 13", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["13"], "solution": "13"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 9295, 2003, 11, 566, 686, 6177, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 315, 55714, 566, 1521], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 5005, 1790, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 566, 1521, 419, 2003, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1657, 55714, 525, 2115, 311, 6177, 1283, 1790, 2003, 13, 88190, 11]}
