er is $\\boxed{40}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?", "answer": "The total number of hours that Rafael has worked by Tuesday is 8+10 = <<8+10=18>>18 hours.\nTo complete his assigned work hours, Rafael works 20 hours more, making his total weekly hours to be 18+20 = <<38=38>>38 hours.\nSince he is paid $20 per hour, he makes $20*38 = $<<20*38=760>>760 a week.\n#### 760", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["760"], "solution": "760"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 54400, 4278, 220, 16, 15, 4115, 389, 7014, 323, 220, 23, 4115, 389, 7589, 389, 806, 9691, 2618, 13, 3085, 220, 17, 15, 4115, 2115, 311, 975, 304, 279, 2003, 11, 1246, 1753, 3220, 1558, 54400, 1281], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 54400, 4278, 220, 16, 15, 4115, 389, 7014, 323, 220, 23, 4115, 389, 7589, 13, 2055, 11, 1156, 11, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1657, 4115, 566, 594, 2669, 3238, 13, 30370, 1846, 3786, 11, 220, 16, 15, 5519, 220, 23, 16819, 220, 16, 23, 4115, 13, 2938, 4977, 1290, 382, 7039, 11, 279, 3405]}
