Happy Good Healthy Family has three times C plus two. So, 3*C + 2. Plugging in the value for C, that would be 3*17 + 2.\n\nLet me compute that. 3 times 17 is... 3*10 is 30, 3*7 is 21, so total is 51. Then adding 2 gives 53. Wait, is that right? Let me check again. Multiplying 17 by 3... 17*3 is indeed 51, add 2 to get 53. Yes, that seems correct.\n\nSo, the Happy Good Healthy Family has 53 cows. Now, we need to add that to We the People's 17 cows. So total cows will be 17 + 53. Let me add those numbers. 17 plus 53... 17 + 50 is 67, plus 3 is 70. So total cows would be 70. \n\nWait, let me confirm once more. First, 17 cows from We the People. Happy Family has 3*17 + 2. 3*17 is 51, plus 2 is 53. Adding to 17 gives 17 + 53 = 70. Yeah, that seems right. Hmm. Are there any steps I might have missed? Let me check the problem statement again. It says \"take to a ranch to graze together\"—so they'll be together, so we need to add them. The numbers are confirmed. So the answer should be 70, which is \\boxed{70}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the problem:\n\n1. Determine the number of cows in the Happy Good Healthy Family:  \n   $3 \\times 17 + 2 = 51 + 2 = 53$.\n\n2. Add the cows from both groups:  \n   $17 + 53 = 70$.\n\nThe total number of cows in the ranch is $\\boxed{70}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "We the People has 17 cows. Happy Good Healthy Family has two more than three times the number of cows We the People has. If their cows are taken to a ranch to graze together, how many cows will be in the ranch altogether?", "answer": "Three times the number of cows We the People has is 3*17=<<3*17=51>>51 cows.\nHappy Good Healthy Family has two more than three times the number of cows We the People has, a total of 51+2=53 cows.\nIf the cows are taken to a ranch to graze together, their total will be 53+17=<<53+17=70>>70 cows.\n#### 70", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: We the People has 17 cows. Happy Good Healthy Family has two more than three times the number of cows We the People has. If their cows are taken to a ranch to graze together, how many cows will be in the ranch altogether?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["70"], "solution": "70"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 1205, 279, 8853, 702, 220, 16, 22, 45166, 13, 23355, 7684, 43354, 12238, 702, 1378, 803, 1091, 2326, 3039, 279, 1372, 315, 45166, 1205, 279, 8853, 702, 13, 1416, 862, 45166, 525, 4429, 311, 264, 38061, 311], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 6771, 752, 1191, 553, 8660, 1128, 279, 3491, 2727, 13, 4710, 1654, 279, 8853, 702, 220, 16, 22, 45166, 13, 5005, 11, 279, 23355, 7684, 43354, 12238, 702, 1378, 803, 1091, 2326, 3039, 279, 1372, 315, 45166, 1205, 279, 8853, 702, 13, 576, 3405, 374, 10161, 1246]}
