 10 more than half the number in Mrs. Finley's class. How many students are in Mr. Johnson's class?", "answer": "Half the number in Mrs. Finley's class is 24/2=<<24/2=12>>12.\nMr. Johnson has 12+10=<<12+10=22>>22 students.\n#### 22", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Mrs. Finley's class has 24 students, and Mr. Johnson's class has 10 more than half the number in Mrs. Finley's class. How many students are in Mr. Johnson's class?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["22"], "solution": "22"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 17618, 13, 5649, 3179, 594, 536, 702, 220, 17, 19, 4143, 11, 323, 4392, 13, 11351, 594, 536, 702, 220, 16, 15, 803, 1091, 4279, 279, 1372, 304, 17618, 13, 5649, 3179, 594, 536, 13, 2585, 1657], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 429, 17618, 13, 5649, 3179, 594, 536, 702, 220, 17, 19, 4143, 13, 5005, 11, 4392, 13, 11351, 594, 536, 702, 220, 16, 15, 803, 1091, 4279, 279, 1372, 304, 17618, 13, 5649, 3179, 594, 536, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1657, 4143, 525, 304, 4392, 13, 11351, 594, 536, 13]}
