hite = 30% = 0.3N\n\nBut we know that the number of red bellied minnows is 20. So:\n\n0.4N = 20\n\nTherefore, N = 20 / 0.4 = 50\n\nSo total minnows are 50. Then white bellies would be 0.3 * 50 = 15. So the answer should be 15 minnows with white bellies. Let me check if that makes sense. If there are 50 minnows, 40 have red, 30 have green, and 30 white. Yes, 50 is total. So 30% of total is 15. So \\boxed{15} is the answer. Hmm, but wait, let me make sure there are no steps I missed.\n\nAlternative approach: Maybe convert percentages to decimals. 40% is 0.4, 30% is 0.3, so white is 100 - 40 -30 = 30% as mentioned. So if there are 20 minnows with red, then how much of 20 is white? Since white is 30% of total, so 30% of total = 15. Therefore, if total is 50, multiplying 0.3*50=15. So yeah, 15 is correct. So the answer is \\boxed{15}.\n</think>\n\nThe solution is to calculate the percentage of minnows that have white bellies, which is 30%, and then find 30% of the total minnows. Since 20 minnows have red bellies, and 40% are red, the total number of minnows is 50. Therefore, 15 minnows have white bellies. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{15}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Mary is counting the number of minnows in the pond. 40% of the minnows have red bellies, 30% have green bellies and the rest have white bellies. If 20 minnows have red bellies, how many minnows have white bellies?", "answer": "First find the total number of minnows by dividing the number of red minnows by the percentage of minnows that are red: 20 minnows / 40% = 50 minnows\nThen subtract the percentages of red- and green-bellied minnows to find the percentage of white-bellied minnows: 100% - 40% - 30% = 30%\nThen multiply the total number of minnows by the percentage that have white bellies: 30% * 50 minnows = <<30*.01*50=15>>15 minnows\n#### 15", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Mary is counting the number of minnows in the pond. 40% of the minnows have red bellies, 30% have green bellies and the rest have white bellies. If 20 minnows have red bellies, how many minnows have white bellies?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["15"], "solution": "15"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 10244, 374, 25009, 279, 1372, 315, 1308, 3328, 82, 304, 279, 35570, 13, 220, 19, 15, 4, 315, 279, 1308, 3328, 82, 614, 2518, 28419, 550, 11, 220, 18, 15, 4, 614, 6176, 28419, 550, 323, 279], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 419, 3491, 700, 13, 2055, 11, 10244, 374, 25009, 1308, 3328, 82, 304, 264, 35570, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 429, 220, 19, 15, 4, 614, 2518, 28419, 550, 11, 220, 18, 15, 4, 614, 6176, 28419, 550, 11, 323, 279, 2732, 614, 4158, 28419, 550, 13, 1597, 1052, 525, 220, 17, 15, 1308, 3328, 82]}
