h isn't too involved here, this should be straightforward. So the answer is \\boxed{14}.\n</think>\n\n$$\n\\boxed{14}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["14"], "solution": "14"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 55843, 702, 10636, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 323, 14816, 9071, 2348, 5248, 74424, 13, 1260, 14816, 678, 315, 279, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 220, 17, 19531, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 1030, 220, 21, 9071, 11, 1221, 14816], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 2055, 55843, 374, 304, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 13, 1260, 702, 2814, 1045, 9071, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 566, 2765, 678, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 1378, 19531, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 1030, 220, 21, 9071, 13, 5005, 566, 14816, 4279, 315, 279, 220, 19, 9071, 304, 279, 1537, 4778, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246]}
