so 3 * 10 = 30 snapdragons.\n\nLilies: 6 per arrangement, therefore 6 * 10 = 60 lilies.\n\nAdding them all together: 80 + 120 + 30 + 60. Let me do that math: 80 + 120 is 200, plus 30 is 230, plus 60 is 290. So total flowers needed are 290. Therefore, the answer is \\boxed{290}.\n</think>\n\n\\boxed{290}<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Marta is arranging floral centerpieces for a reception party.  Each arrangement needs to have 8 roses,12 daisies, 3 snapdragons and twice as many lilies.  The reception will have 10 tables.  How many flowers will she need in total to fill this order?", "answer": "She needs twice as many lilies as the 3 snapdragons in the arrangement so she needs 2*3 = <<2*3=6>>6 lilies\nShe needs 8 roses, 12 daisies, 3 snapdragons and 6 lilies for a total of 8+12+3+6 = <<8+12+3+6=29>>29 flowers per arrangement\nShe needs 29 flowers per each of the 10 tables for a total of 29*10 = <<29*10=290>>290 flowers\n#### 290", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Marta is arranging floral centerpieces for a reception party.  Each arrangement needs to have 8 roses,12 daisies, 3 snapdragons and twice as many lilies.  The reception will have 10 tables.  How many flowers will she need in total to fill this order?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["290"], "solution": "290"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 8127, 64, 374, 76118, 45019, 4126, 46468, 369, 264, 23117, 4614, 13, 220, 8886, 26112, 3880, 311, 614, 220, 23, 60641, 11, 16, 17, 294, 2782, 550, 11, 220, 18, 10658, 33931, 2382, 323, 10917, 438, 1657], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 8127, 64, 3880, 311, 30893, 1059, 45019, 4126, 46468, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 1817, 26112, 702, 220, 23, 60641, 11, 220, 16, 17, 294, 2782, 550, 11, 220,