ter Farms. So that's 3*45 = 135 chickens.\n4. Boudin Butchers donated one-third of the number of dressed chickens that Hormel donated. Hormel has 135, so Boudin Butchers have 1/3 of that, which is 135/3 = 45.\n5. Del Monte Foods donated 30 fewer bottles of water than American Summits. American Summits has 90 bottled water, so Del Monte has 90 - 30 = 60 bottles.\n\nNow, I need to add up all the items donated by each company to find the total.\n\nFoster Farms: 45 dressed chickens.\n\nAmerican Summits: 90 bottled water.\n\nHormel: 135 dressed chickens.\n\nBoudin Butchers: 45 dressed chickens.\n\nDel Monte: 60 bottles of water.\n\nAdding them together:\n\nDressed chickens: 45 (Foster) + 135 (Hormel) + 45 (Boudin) = 45 + 135 is 180, plus 45 makes 225.\n\nBottled water: 90 (AIS) + 60 (Del Monte) = 150.\n\nTotal food items would be 225 (chickens) + 150 (water) = 375. So the answer should be \\boxed{375}.\n\nWait, let me double-check calculations to be sure.\n\nFoster: 45\n\nAIS: 2*45 = 90\n\nHormel: 3*45 = 135\n\nBoudin: 1/3 of Hormel's 135 is 45.\n\nDel Monte: 90 - 30 = 60.\n\nTotal chickens: 45 + 135 + 45 = 225. Wait, 45+135 is 180, plus 45 is 225. Correct.\n\nTotal water: 90 + 60 = 150. Then total is 225 + 150 = 375. Yes, that's correct. So the final answer is \\boxed{375}.\n</think>\n\n$$\n\\boxed{375}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Five food companies sponsored a local food bank. Foster Farms donated 45 dressed chickens; American Summits donated twice the number of bottled water than the number of dressed chicken donated by Foster Farms; Hormel donated three times the number of dressed chickens that Foster Farms donated; Boudin Butchers donated one-third of the number of dressed chickens that Hormel donated; Del Monte Foods donated 30 fewer bottles of water than American Summits. How many food items did the companies donate in total?", "answer": "American Summits donated 45 x 2 = <<45*2=90>>90 bottled waters.\nHormel donated 45 x 3 = <<45*3=135>>135 spams.\nBoudin Bakery donated 135 x 1/3 = <<135*1/3=45>>45 sourdoughs.\nDel Monte Foods donated 90 - 30 = <<90-30=60>>60 canned fruits.\nTherefore, a total of 45 + 90 + 135 + 45 + 60 = <<45+90+135+45+60=375>>375 different food.\n#### 375", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Five food companies sponsored a local food bank. Foster Farms donated 45 dressed chickens; American Summits donated twice the number of bottled water than the number of dressed chicken donated by Foster Farms; Hormel donated three times the number of dressed chickens that Foster Farms donated; Boudin Butchers donated one-third of the number of dressed chickens that Hormel donated; Del Monte Foods donated 30 fewer bottles of water than American Summits. How many food items did the companies donate in total?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["375"], "solution": "375"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 20924, 3607, 5110, 29538, 264, 2205, 3607, 6073, 13, 38174, 67021, 33368, 220, 19, 20, 25365, 53523, 26, 3693, 8116, 44703, 33368, 10917, 279, 1372, 315, 71078, 3015, 1091, 279, 1372, 315, 25365, 16158, 33368, 553, 38174], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1430, 311, 11625, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 88190, 11, 1052, 525, 4236, 3607, 5110, 60859, 3607, 3589, 13, 6771, 752, 1140, 700, 279, 1995, 2661, 1447, 16, 13, 38174, 67021, 33368, 220, 19, 20, 25365, 53523, 624, 17, 13, 3693, 8116, 44703, 33368, 10917, 438, 1657, 71078, 3015, 438, 38174, 67021, 13, 2055, 421, 38174, 67021]}
