 insurance cover is 5% of her earnings. Similarly, 5% of $420. 5% is 0.05, so 0.05 * 420. Let me calculate that. 420 times 0.05. Well, 420 divided by 20 is 21, so 0.05 is one-tenth of 20, so 420 divided by 20 is 21. Therefore, insurance is $21.\n\nThen, the union dues are $5. So, the total deductions would be $84 (tax) + $21 (insurance) + $5 (union) equals $110. \n\nTherefore, Vikki takes home her total earnings after these deductions, which would be $420 minus $110. Let me subtract 110 from 420. 420 minus 100 is 320, minus another 10 is 310. So her take home is $310, which is $\\boxed{310}$.\n</think>\n\n\\boxed{310}<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Vikki worked 42 hours in one week. Her hourly pay rate is $10. From her weekly earnings, 20% is deducted as tax, 5% is deducted as insurance cover, and $5 is deducted for union dues. How much money, in dollars, does Vikki take home after deductions?", "answer": "Vikki earnt 10 × $42 = $<<10*42=420>>420 in one week.\nShe then gets taxed $420 × 0.2 = $<<420*0.2=84>>84.\nShe also loses $420 × 0.05 = $<<420*0.05=21>>21 due to insurance.\nVikki also pays $5 in union dues.\nIn total Vikki loses $84 + $21 + $5 = $<<84+21+5=110>>110 because of deductions.\nHer final total pay after deductions is $420 - $110 = $<<420-110=310>>310\n#### 310", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Vikki worked 42 hours in one week. Her hourly pay rate is $10. From her weekly earnings, 20% is deducted as tax, 5% is deducted as insurance cover, and $5 is deducted for union dues. How much money, in dollars, does Vikki take home after deductions?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["310"], "solution": "310"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 28376, 6642, 6439, 220, 19, 17, 4115, 304, 825, 2003, 13, 6252, 46629, 2291, 4379, 