ided by 30 equals 4 boxes. 4 boxes times $8 is $32. Therefore, the answer should be $\\boxed{32}$.\n</think>\n\nThe solution involves calculating the total number of coffee pods needed and then determining the cost based on the box price. \n\n1. Total coffee pods needed: 3 pods/day * 40 days = 120 pods.\n2. Number of boxes required: 120 pods / 30 pods/box = 4 boxes.\n3. Total cost: 4 boxes * $8.00/box = $32.00.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{32}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Sharon’s vacation rental has a Keurig coffee machine.  She will be there for 40 days.  She has 3 cups of coffee (3 coffee pods) every morning.  Her coffee pods come 30 pods to a box for $8.00.  How much will she spend on coffee to last her for the entire vacation?", "answer": "She'll be on vacation for 40 days and drinks 3 cups of coffee/pods per day for a total of 40*3 = <<40*3=120>>120 coffee pods\nHer coffee pods come 30 in a box and she needs 120 coffee pods so that’s 120/30 = <<120/30=4>>4 boxes\nEach box costs $8.00 and she needs 4 boxes so that’s 8*4 = $<<8*4=32.00>>32.00\n#### 32", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Sharon’s vacation rental has a Keurig coffee machine.  She will be there for 40 days.  She has 3 cups of coffee (3 coffee pods) every morning.  Her coffee pods come 30 pods to a box for $8.00.  How much will she spend on coffee to last her for the entire vacation?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["32"], "solution": "32"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 51852, 748, 20161, 18645, 702, 264, 6569, 324, 343, 10799, 5662, 13, 220, 2932, 686, 387, 1052, 369, 220, 19, 15, 2849, 13, 220, 2932, 702, 220, 18, 25374, 315, 10799, 320, 18, 10799, 54587, 8, 1449], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 576, 3491, 374, 911, 51852, 19211, 3