ng the fourth game's 10 points gives 30 + 10 = 40. \n\nWait, let me double-check. The average of the first three games is 10, so that must mean the fourth game is 10 points. Adding those together, 10 + 14 + 6 + 10. That should be 40. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be \\boxed{40}, which corresponds to the total points.\n</think>\n\nThe total points Clayton scored during the first four games is \\boxed{40}.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Clayton plays basketball on a team. He has played three games so far. In the first game, he scored 10 points. In the second game, he scored 14 points. In the third game, he scored 6 points. In the fourth game, he scored the average of his points from the first three games.  How many total points did Clayton score during the first four games?", "answer": "During the first three games Clayton scored 10 points + 14 + 6 = <<10+14+6=30>>30 points.\nThe average for Clayton's first three games is 30 points / 3 = <<30/3=10>>10 points per game.\nFor the first four games, Clayton scored 30 points + 10 points = <<30+10=40>>40 points.\n#### 40", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Clayton plays basketball on a team. He has played three games so far. In the first game, he scored 10 points. In the second game, he scored 14 points. In the third game, he scored 6 points. In the fourth game, he scored the average of his points from the first three games.  How many total points did Clayton score during the first four games?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["40"], "solution": "40"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 63444, 11088, 19240, 389, 264, 2083, 13, 1260, 702, 6342, 2326, 3868, 773, 3041, 13, 758, 279, 1156, 1809, 11, 566, 16548, 220, 16, 15, 3501, 13, 758, 279, 2086, 1809, 11, 566, 16548, 220, 16, 19], "respon