nd?", "answer": "Alexander spends 5 * $1 = $<<5*1=5>>5 on apples.\nHe spends 2 * $2 = $<<2*2=4>>4 on oranges.\nIn total, he spends $5 + $4 = $<<5+4=9>>9.\n#### 9", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Alexander is going food shopping. If he buys 5 apples for $1 each and 2 oranges for $2 each, how much does he spend?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["9"], "solution": "9"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 20042, 374, 2087, 3607, 11919, 13, 1416, 566, 49531, 220, 20, 40676, 369, 400, 16, 1817, 323, 220, 17, 84038, 369, 400, 17, 1817, 11, 1246, 1753, 1558, 566, 8329, 5267, 36842, 25, 151645, 198, 151644, 77091], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 20042, 374, 11919, 369, 40676, 323, 84038, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 566, 49531, 220, 20, 40676, 369, 400, 16, 1817, 323, 220, 17, 84038, 369, 400, 17, 1817, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1753, 566, 37102, 304, 2790, 382, 5338, 11, 358, 1265, 7071, 700, 279, 2783, 369, 279, 40676, 13, 8704, 1052, 525]}
