gle: length 3, width 6. Area = 3*6 = 18. Square: side 5, area 5*5 = 25. Difference is 25-18=7. That seems right. Therefore, \\boxed{7} is the answer.\n</think>\n\nThe difference in area between the rectangle and the square is \\boxed{7}.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "A rectangle has a length of 3 inches and a width of 6 inches. A square has a width of 5 inches. What is the difference in area between the two shapes?", "answer": "The area of the rectangle is 3 x 6 = <<3*6=18>>18 sq in\nThe area of the square is 5 x 5 = <<5*5=25>>25 sq in\nThe difference is 25 - 18 = <<25-18=7>>7 sq in\n#### 7", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: A rectangle has a length of 3 inches and a width of 6 inches. A square has a width of 5 inches. What is the difference in area between the two shapes?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["7"], "solution": "7"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 362, 22756, 702, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 18, 14924, 323, 264, 2374, 315, 220, 21, 14924, 13, 362, 9334, 702, 264, 2374, 315, 220, 20, 14924, 13, 3555, 374, 279, 6672, 304, 3082, 1948, 279, 1378, 20816], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 279, 6672, 304, 3082, 1948, 264, 22756, 323, 264, 9334, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 279, 22756, 702, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 18, 14924, 323, 264, 2374, 315, 220, 21, 14924, 13, 13824, 11, 3331, 389, 13, 1416, 432, 594, 264, 22756, 11, 14279, 11, 3084, 323, 2374, 525, 279, 14002, 11067, 13]}
