oblem states he was not able to pay on time for his balance worth $150. If the balance is $150, and he hasn't paid yet, then a finance charge of 2% would mean that he's owed 2% of $150. So total amount due would be $150 * 1.02. Let me compute that again. 1.02 * 150. 150 * 1 is 150, 150 * 0.02 is 3, so total is 153. Yes, so he pays $153 in total. Therefore, the answer is $\\boxed{153}$. I think that's correct.\n</think>\n\nThe problem states that Mr. Smith has a balance of $150 with a 2% finance charge. To calculate his total payment, we first determine the amount owed as $150 * (1 + 0.02) = $153. Hence, the amount he will pay is $\\boxed{153}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Mr. Smith has incurred a 2% finance charge because he was not able to pay on time for his balance worth $150. If he plans to settle his balance today, how much will Mr. Smith pay?", "answer": "The finance charge amounts to $150 x 2/100 = $<<150*2/100=3>>3.\nThus, Mr. Smith will pay a total of $150 + $3 = $<<150+3=153>>153.\n#### 153", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Mr. Smith has incurred a 2% finance charge because he was not able to pay on time for his balance worth $150. If he plans to settle his balance today, how much will Mr. Smith pay?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["153"], "solution": "153"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 4392, 13, 9082, 702, 51772, 264, 220, 17, 4, 17017, 6757, 1576, 566, 572, 537, 2952, 311, 2291, 389, 882, 369, 806, 8172, 5802, 400, 16, 20, 15, 13, 1416, 566, 6649, 311, 24729, 806, 8172, 3351], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 2055, 279, 3491, 374, 429, 4392, 13, 9082, 702, 264, 8172, 5802, 400, 16, 20, 15, 323, 566, 1030, 264, 220, 17, 4, 17017, 6757, 1576, 566, 3207, 944, 2291, 389, 882, 13,